BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:What We Inherit\, What We Create\; Collage as Reflection
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260516T160000
UID:a57cfef4459ed325d7c9e696db4e38f1@petalumaartscenter.org
DESCRIPTION:In dialogue with our upcoming Origin Stories exhibition\, this
  workshop uses found imagery\, vintage ephemera\, and contemporary materia
 ls to reflect on memory\, place\, and the textures of everyday life. Parti
 cipants will create layered works that balance personal narrative with bro
 ader cultural reference. Emphasis will be placed on editing\, composition\
 , and allowing materials to suggest meaning rather than working toward a f
 ixed outcome. All experience levels are welcome. Instructors : Robin Borel
 li\, Laura Engdahl\, and Jen Siddens May 16\, 2026 12:00pm – 4:00pm $150
  Members\, $170 Non-Members Materials : Two 12” x 12” wood panels and 
 heavy art paper&nbsp\;are provided and included in the price.&nbsp\; A sup
 ply list of other art supplies for participants to bring will be provided 
 upon registration.&nbsp\;Participants are also encouraged to bring copies 
 of personal photographs\, letters\, maps\, or printed matter that feel con
 nected to their own sense of personal history\, though some shared collage
  materials will also be provided. #block-7a14000312225e29e91d { } #block-7
